# Next.js Frontend Quality

- Inspect package.json and current framework conventions before adding libraries.
- Preserve the existing router and data-fetching architecture unless a migration is explicitly approved.
- Prefer small composable components over page-sized monoliths.
- Keep static content server-rendered where the current architecture supports it; use client components only for genuine interaction.
- Avoid unnecessary global state.
- Use semantic HTML and accessible interactive controls.
- Use `next/image` where appropriate and prevent avoidable layout shift.
- Lazy-load below-fold rich media.
- Do not silently swallow frontend data errors.
- Reuse project fetch/query abstractions.
- After material edits run the existing lint, typecheck, tests and build commands discovered from package.json.
- Do not invent commands or replace the package manager.
